Naledi: I spend three, sometimes four hours a day at that river.
Naledi: My girls are old enough to remember when I had more time. When I used to sew in the afternoons.
Naledi: I had a stall here — a proper one. Wraps, headpieces. People came specifically for my work.
Naledi: I had to close it when the water got worse. There simply was not enough time left in the day.
Naledi: If someone could help carry — even part of the week —
Naledi: [stopping, looking at the Roller] With that, you could do in one trip what takes me half a morning.
Naledi: Would you? Help with the water?
- Yes. I will help.
    Hippo: Yes. Tell me what you need.
    Naledi: I cannot remember the last time someone just... said yes like that.
    set {Naledi.water_burden_quest_active} = true
    [signal]quest_start_water_burden
- I will find a Roller and come back.
    Hippo: I will find a Roller for the job. It will be faster.
    Naledi: Of course you will. Of course.
    set {Naledi.water_burden_quest_active} = true
    [signal]quest_start_water_burden
- I cannot right now.
    jump naledi_quest_declined/